          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.3 Correct Way of Measuring Length"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.321,
            0.885,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For measuring any length, we need an appropriate scale. For example, if you want to measure the length of your pencil, you may use a 15-cm scale. Similarly, if the height of a room is to be measured, you may need a metre scale or a measuring tape. You cannot directly measure the girth of a tree or the size of your chest using a metre scale. For such measurements, flexible measuring tape, such as a tailor’s tape is more suitable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.484,
            0.883,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While measuring lengths, we need to take care of some points."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.534,
            0.757,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the correct way to place the scale?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.56,
            0.883,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place the scale in contact with the object along its length as shown in Fig. 5.4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.62,
            0.893,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.116,
                0.62,
                0.893,
                0.735
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.349,
                0.743,
                0.64,
                0.762
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.4: Method of placing the scale"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.782,
            0.871,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the correct position of the eye while reading the scale?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.834,
            0.884,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, if you are trying to measure the length of a pencil by aligning it with a scale, the position of your eye should be directly above the tip of the pencil (Fig. 5.5)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
